<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.0">
  <POU Name="FB_HomePlc" Id="{9272de4d-31c0-45f3-945b-64e071908fad}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_HomePlc
(*
    Homing option 1, PLC-based (references/homing.md): search the
    reference switch with MC_MoveVelocity, stop with MC_Halt, then shift
    the position so the switch edge becomes the reference position.

    Two options, both off unless set:
    - Two-speed search (stParams.fSlowVelocity > 0): find the switch at
      fSearchVelocity, move off it again, then approach it at
      fSlowVelocity. Only the slow edge sets the position.
    - Reversal at a limit (bSearchLimitOk wired): a search that reaches
      the limit in its direction stops, travels the other way through
      the switch until it is released, and searches again, so the edge
      is always approached from the same side. Once per run; a second
      limit is cErrLimit.

    It marks the axis homed in one of two ways (stParams.bMarkNcHomed):
      FALSE  own flag. bHomed is the record; ST_AxisStatus.Homed is not
             touched, so an HMI reading the NC's flag sees "not homed".
      TRUE   NC homed state. MC_Home with MC_ForceCalibration at the end;
             bHomed mirrors Axis.Status.Homed, which is the one record.
    Either way a run starts by clearing the mark, so a failed or aborted
    run leaves the axis "not homed", never homed on a half-set position.
    The NC mark is cleared and set by explicit MC_Home calls; nothing
    here relies on MC_SetPosition changing it, or leaving it alone.

    TEMPLATE - built and run on a simulated axis (4024.55), not on a real
    one; the two options and the run timeout not even that yet. Test it
    on your axis at reduced velocity and torque. A reference switch is
    not a safety device; homing is not safe homing.

    CONTRACT
    - Call every cycle, unconditionally. bExecute is edge-triggered;
      bDone / bError hold until bExecute falls (one scan if it already
      fell). A falling bExecute does not stop a run: halt the axis
      (FB_Axis.Halt) and this block reports cErrAborted.
    - The axis must be enabled (MC_Power, e.g. FB_Axis) and nothing else
      may command it during the run.
    - bRefSwitch is the switch's input, every cycle; TRUE = on the switch.
    - bSearchLimitOk: the limit switch in the search direction, NC
      contact, TRUE = not at the limit (as ST_AxisMachineIn). Left
      unconnected it stays TRUE and the run never reverses. The axis must
      reach the limit without an axis error: an error ends the run.
    - The switch must stay active for longer than the braking distance
      of the search. If the axis overshoots it, the next search goes the
      wrong way and ends at the limit (reversal) or the step timeout.
    - bHomed is not retained: after a restart the axis is not homed.
      With stParams.bUnhomeOnAxisError, any axis error clears the own
      flag too (bMarkNcHomed FALSE only).
    - Two timeouts: tStepTimeout for each step, tRunTimeout for the whole
      run. The run limit catches a loop of short steps, such as a
      chattering switch cycling MoveOff -> HaltOff -> CheckSwitch.

    ACCURACY
    The PLC sees the edge, so the position is taken in the scan the input
    changes: within one PLC cycle x search velocity of the true edge, plus
    the input's filter time, plus a cycle's lag when the PLC task runs
    slower than the NC task. The shift is relative (MC_SetPosition Mode
    TRUE) by fReferencePosition - position at the edge, so the braking
    distance does not end up in the zero. Search slowly, or use the
    two-speed search to keep a long search short; for better, latch the
    edge in hardware (touch probe, homing option 4).
*)
VAR_INPUT
    bExecute       : BOOL;              // rising edge starts a homing run
    bRefSwitch     : BOOL;              // reference switch input, every cycle
    bSearchLimitOk : BOOL := TRUE;      // FALSE = at the limit, search side
    stParams       : ST_HomePlcParams;  // read when bExecute rises
END_VAR
VAR_IN_OUT
    Axis       : AXIS_REF;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    bBusy    : BOOL;
    bDone    : BOOL;               // homed; holds until bExecute falls
    bError   : BOOL;
    nErrorID : UDINT;              // NC code (scripts/nc_error.py) or cErr
    bHomed   : BOOL;               // the homed mark, see above
END_VAR
VAR
    eState       : E_HomePlcState := E_HomePlcState.Idle;
    eStatePrev   : E_HomePlcState := E_HomePlcState.Idle;
    bStepChanged : BOOL;           // TRUE the one scan a step is entered
    bTimedStep   : BOOL;
    stRun        : ST_HomePlcParams;  // stParams, frozen at the start
    eMoveOffDir  : MC_Direction := MC_Direction.MC_Positive_Direction;
    eHomeMode    : MC_HomingMode := MC_HomingMode.MC_ResetCalibration;
    fPosAtEdge   : LREAL;          // actual position when the edge came
    bSlowPass    : BOOL;           // two-speed search: now the slow one
    bReversed    : BOOL;           // this run has reversed at a limit
    bSwitchSeen  : BOOL;           // Reverse: the switch has come

    fbExecTrig   : R_TRIG;
    fbSwitchTrig : R_TRIG;
    fbStepTimer  : TON;
    fbRunTimer   : TON;            // the whole run, never re-armed by a step
    fbMoveOff    : MC_MoveVelocity;  // MoveOff and Reverse, away from it
    fbSearch     : MC_MoveVelocity;
    fbHalt       : MC_Halt;
    fbSetPos     : MC_SetPosition;
    fbHome       : MC_Home;        // calibration flag only, no movement
    stSetPosOpt  : ST_SetPositionOptions;
END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    // Own codes sit above 16#FFFF, clear of every NC and ADS code.
    cErrParams       : UDINT := 16#0001_0101;  // stParams not usable
    cErrMoveOffTime  : UDINT := 16#0001_0102;  // switch not released
    cErrSearchTime   : UDINT := 16#0001_0103;  // switch not found
    cErrStepTime     : UDINT := 16#0001_0104;  // halt / set / mark slow
    cErrAborted      : UDINT := 16#0001_0105;  // another command took over
    cErrRunTime      : UDINT := 16#0001_0106;  // whole run too long
    cErrLimit        : UDINT := 16#0001_0107;  // limit again after reversing
    cErrInvalidState : UDINT := 16#0001_01FF;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[// Sensors above the CASE, so it decides on this scan's values. Reading
// the status again is harmless if FB_Axis already did; this block does
// not depend on being called after it.
Axis.ReadStatus();
fbExecTrig(CLK := bExecute);
fbSwitchTrig(CLK := bRefSwitch);

bStepChanged := (eState <> eStatePrev);
eStatePrev   := eState;
bTimedStep   := (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Idle)
                AND (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Done)
                AND (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Error);
// One timer for every step: IN low on the scan a step is entered re-arms
// it, so each step gets a full timeout (twincat-st FB_Sequence shape).
fbStepTimer(IN := bTimedStep AND NOT bStepChanged,
            PT := stRun.tStepTimeout);
// The run timer only re-arms between runs (Idle, Done, Error).
fbRunTimer(IN := bTimedStep, PT := stRun.tRunTimeout);

CASE eState OF

    E_HomePlcState.Idle:
        IF fbExecTrig.Q THEN
            stRun    := stParams;
            nErrorID := 0;
            eState   := E_HomePlcState.Prepare;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.Prepare:
        bHomed      := FALSE;
        bSlowPass   := FALSE;
        bReversed   := FALSE;
        bSwitchSeen := FALSE;
        IF NOT M_ParamsOk() THEN
            M_Fail(errorID := cErrParams, bStop := FALSE);
        ELSE
            IF stRun.eSearchDirection = MC_Direction.MC_Positive_Direction
            THEN
                eMoveOffDir := MC_Direction.MC_Negative_Direction;
            ELSE
                eMoveOffDir := MC_Direction.MC_Positive_Direction;
            END_IF
            IF stRun.bMarkNcHomed THEN
                eHomeMode := MC_HomingMode.MC_ResetCalibration;
                eState    := E_HomePlcState.ClearNcHomed;
            ELSE
                eState := E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch;
            END_IF
        END_IF

    // Each moving or waiting step: M_StepResult is TRUE when the step's
    // own condition is met; on an error, an abort by another command, the
    // step timeout or the run timeout it has already moved to Stopping or
    // Error.
    E_HomePlcState.ClearNcHomed:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbHome.Done,
                        bErr := fbHome.Error, nErr := fbHome.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbHome.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch;
        END_IF

    // The hub between moves: on the switch, move off it; at the limit
    // ahead, the switch is behind the axis, so reverse (once); else search.
    E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch:
        IF bRefSwitch THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.MoveOff;
        ELSIF NOT bSearchLimitOk AND bReversed THEN
            M_Fail(errorID := cErrLimit, bStop := FALSE);
        ELSIF NOT bSearchLimitOk THEN
            bReversed   := TRUE;
            bSwitchSeen := FALSE;
            eState      := E_HomePlcState.Reverse;
        ELSE
            eState := E_HomePlcState.Search;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.MoveOff:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := NOT bRefSwitch,
                        bErr := fbMoveOff.Error, nErr := fbMoveOff.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbMoveOff.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrMoveOffTime, bStop := TRUE) THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.HaltOff;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.HaltOff:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbHalt.Done,
                        bErr := fbHalt.Error, nErr := fbHalt.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbHalt.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            // check again: a bouncing switch can read "released" while the
            // axis is still on it, and Search would then never see an edge
            eState := E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch;
        END_IF

    // Back the way it came, at search speed, until the switch has come
    // and gone again: the axis then stands on the side the search starts.
    E_HomePlcState.Reverse:
        IF bRefSwitch THEN
            bSwitchSeen := TRUE;
        END_IF
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := bSwitchSeen AND NOT bRefSwitch,
                        bErr := fbMoveOff.Error, nErr := fbMoveOff.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbMoveOff.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrSearchTime, bStop := TRUE) THEN
            // HaltOff then CheckSwitch, as after MoveOff: a bounce that
            // read "released" too early ends in MoveOff, the same way
            eState := E_HomePlcState.HaltOff;
        END_IF

    // A limit first: the switch is then behind the axis, and an error the
    // limit causes on this move must not end the run before it reverses.
    E_HomePlcState.Search:
        IF NOT bSearchLimitOk THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.HaltLimit;
        ELSIF M_StepResult(bDone := fbSwitchTrig.Q,
                           bErr := fbSearch.Error, nErr := fbSearch.ErrorID,
                           bAborted := fbSearch.CommandAborted,
                           nTimeoutErr := cErrSearchTime, bStop := TRUE) THEN
            // the position in the scan the edge is seen, before the halt
            fPosAtEdge := Axis.NcToPlc.ActPos;
            eState     := E_HomePlcState.HaltSearch;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.HaltLimit:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbHalt.Done,
                        bErr := fbHalt.Error, nErr := fbHalt.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbHalt.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch;   // reverses from there
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.HaltSearch:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbHalt.Done,
                        bErr := fbHalt.Error, nErr := fbHalt.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbHalt.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            IF (stRun.fSlowVelocity > 0.0) AND NOT bSlowPass THEN
                // fast pass done: off the switch again, then the slow one
                bSlowPass := TRUE;
                eState    := E_HomePlcState.CheckSwitch;
            ELSE
                eState := E_HomePlcState.SetPosition;
            END_IF
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.SetPosition:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbSetPos.Done,
                        bErr := fbSetPos.Error, nErr := fbSetPos.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := FALSE,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            IF stRun.bMarkNcHomed THEN
                eHomeMode := MC_HomingMode.MC_ForceCalibration;
                eState    := E_HomePlcState.MarkNcHomed;
            ELSE
                bHomed := TRUE;
                eState := E_HomePlcState.Done;
            END_IF
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.MarkNcHomed:
        IF M_StepResult(bDone := fbHome.Done,
                        bErr := fbHome.Error, nErr := fbHome.ErrorID,
                        bAborted := fbHome.CommandAborted,
                        nTimeoutErr := cErrStepTime, bStop := FALSE) THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.Done;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.Done:
        IF NOT bExecute THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.Idle;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.Stopping:
        // Failed while moving: stop, then report the original error.
        IF fbHalt.Done OR fbHalt.Error OR fbHalt.CommandAborted
           OR fbStepTimer.Q THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.Error;
        END_IF

    E_HomePlcState.Error:
        IF NOT bExecute THEN
            eState := E_HomePlcState.Idle;
        END_IF

ELSE
    M_Fail(errorID := cErrInvalidState, bStop := TRUE);
END_CASE

// Commanded blocks below the CASE, called every scan with the inputs the
// CASE just chose, so a step entered this scan issues its command now.
// Each Execute is TRUE only in its own steps, and no two of a block's
// steps follow each other, so every entry is a fresh rising edge.
stSetPosOpt.ClearPositionLag := TRUE;
fbMoveOff(Axis := Axis,
          Execute := (eState = E_HomePlcState.MoveOff)
                     OR (eState = E_HomePlcState.Reverse),
          Velocity := SEL(eState = E_HomePlcState.Reverse,
                          stRun.fMoveOffVelocity, stRun.fSearchVelocity),
          Direction := eMoveOffDir);
fbSearch(Axis := Axis,
         Execute := (eState = E_HomePlcState.Search),
         Velocity := SEL(bSlowPass,
                         stRun.fSearchVelocity, stRun.fSlowVelocity),
         Direction := stRun.eSearchDirection);
fbHalt(Axis := Axis,
       Execute := (eState = E_HomePlcState.HaltOff)
                  OR (eState = E_HomePlcState.HaltSearch)
                  OR (eState = E_HomePlcState.HaltLimit)
                  OR (eState = E_HomePlcState.Stopping),
       Deceleration := stRun.fDeceleration);
fbSetPos(Axis := Axis,
         Execute := (eState = E_HomePlcState.SetPosition),
         Position := stRun.fReferencePosition - fPosAtEdge,
         Mode := TRUE,                      // relative: shift by Position
         Options := stSetPosOpt);
fbHome(Axis := Axis,
       Execute := (eState = E_HomePlcState.ClearNcHomed)
                  OR (eState = E_HomePlcState.MarkNcHomed),
       HomingMode := eHomeMode);

bBusy  := (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Idle)
          AND (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Done)
          AND (eState <> E_HomePlcState.Error);
bDone  := (eState = E_HomePlcState.Done);
bError := (eState = E_HomePlcState.Error);
IF stRun.bMarkNcHomed THEN
    // Mirror the NC's mark, but not during a run: until ClearNcHomed is
    // through, the NC still shows the old one.
    bHomed := Axis.Status.Homed AND NOT bBusy;
ELSIF stRun.bUnhomeOnAxisError AND Axis.Status.Error THEN
    // The block cannot tell from the code whether the position survived
    // (a lag error usually keeps it, an encoder error may not): drop it.
    bHomed := FALSE;
END_IF
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Method Name="M_ParamsOk" Id="{a72b3be7-0feb-428b-8be3-c7d0f5babcdc}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_ParamsOk : BOOL
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Refuse a run the axis cannot do sensibly, before anything moves. A
// velocity of 0 is an NC error anyway, and a Halt deceleration of 0
// would leave the stop ramp to the library.
M_ParamsOk :=
    ((stRun.eSearchDirection = MC_Direction.MC_Positive_Direction)
     OR (stRun.eSearchDirection = MC_Direction.MC_Negative_Direction))
    AND (stRun.fSearchVelocity > 0.0)
    AND (stRun.fSlowVelocity >= 0.0)          // 0: single-speed search
    AND (stRun.fMoveOffVelocity > 0.0)
    AND (stRun.fDeceleration > 0.0)
    AND (stRun.tStepTimeout > T#0S)
    AND (stRun.tRunTimeout > T#0S);]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_Fail" Id="{f4d90d8f-966c-47f3-b37a-6a3f58b93687}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_Fail
VAR_INPUT
    errorID : UDINT;
    bStop   : BOOL;   // TRUE: this block's move may be running; halt it
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// Not halted on an abort: the axis is then another block's, and halting
// it would fight that block. Not halted after a failed halt either.
nErrorID := errorID;
IF bStop THEN
    eState := E_HomePlcState.Stopping;
ELSE
    eState := E_HomePlcState.Error;
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
    <Method Name="M_StepResult" Id="{49e77785-3dd6-45e4-87f8-a4e323b0bef8}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[METHOD PRIVATE M_StepResult : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    bDone       : BOOL;    // the step's own end condition
    bErr        : BOOL;    // the step block's Error
    nErr        : UDINT;   // and its ErrorID
    bAborted    : BOOL;    // its CommandAborted; FALSE if it has none
    nTimeoutErr : UDINT;   // code to report when the step times out
    bStop       : BOOL;    // TRUE: the step moves the axis; halt on fail
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
      <Implementation>
        <ST><![CDATA[// One step's outcome, checked in priority order: done beats an error
// seen on the same scan, an error beats an abort, all beat the timeouts,
// and the step's own timeout beats the run's.
// An abort means another command owns the axis now, so it never halts.
M_StepResult := FALSE;
IF bDone THEN
    M_StepResult := TRUE;
ELSIF bErr THEN
    M_Fail(errorID := nErr, bStop := bStop);
ELSIF bAborted THEN
    M_Fail(errorID := cErrAborted, bStop := FALSE);
ELSIF fbStepTimer.Q THEN
    M_Fail(errorID := nTimeoutErr, bStop := bStop);
ELSIF fbRunTimer.Q THEN
    M_Fail(errorID := cErrRunTime, bStop := bStop);
END_IF]]></ST>
      </Implementation>
    </Method>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
